}

var _ reauthFunc = driveRunOAuthFlow // driveRunOAuthFlow must match reauthFunc's signature
```

Go's function types are structural, so `driveRunOAuthFlow` is already assignable to a `reauthFunc` parameter without any change to its own declaration — the `var _ reauthFunc = driveRunOAuthFlow` line doesn't change behavior, it's purely a documented, compiler-checked assertion that pins the relationship (same trick as `var _ io.Reader = (*T)(nil)` for interface satisfaction). If either signature drifts, it fails to compile right there instead of surfacing as a confusing error at the `driveClient` call site.

